<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-2">2 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Mercurius becomes Pope John II, the first pope to change his name</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Roman priest Mercurius, reluctant to reign under the name of a pagan god, took the name John II on his consecration. Adopting a papal name later became the settled custom of the Church.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/belisarius" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/belisarius.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-13">13 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Belisarius defeats the Vandal king Gelimer at Ad Decimum</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">At the tenth milestone south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a>, the Byzantine general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belisarius">Belisarius</a> defeated the Vandal army of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gelimer">Gelimer</a>, whose attempt to trap the invaders failed. Belisarius entered Carthage two days later, opening <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/justinian-i">Justinian I</a>'s reconquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ad-decimum">Battle of Ad Decimum</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belisarius">Belisarius</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gelimer">Gelimer</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/belisarius" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/belisarius.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-15">15 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Belisarius defeats the Vandal king Gelimer at Tricamarum</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">West of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a>, the Byzantine army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belisarius">Belisarius</a> defeated the Vandal king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gelimer">Gelimer</a>, whose brother Tzazon was killed. Gelimer fled to the mountains and surrendered in 534, ending the Vandal Kingdom and restoring <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-tricamarum">Battle of Tricamarum</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belisarius">Belisarius</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gelimer">Gelimer</a></div></div></li></ol></section>
